 115  *
 116  * MOST SETS ARE DECLARED AND ELEMENTS ASSIGNED IN THE ORDER LISTED IN THE 
      COMMENTS ABOVE.  HOWEVER,
 117  * SOME SETS ARE ASSIGNED AFTER NECESSARY DATA HAVE BEEN ENTERED.  A GAMS S
      ET IS CALLED DYNAMIC IF
 118  * ITS ELEMENTS ARE ASSIGNED BASED ON THE ELEMENTS OF OTHER SETS OR THE VAL
      UES OF CERTAIN PARAMETERS.
 119  * DYNAMIC SETS ARE MARKED ABOVE WITH **.  ONCE MEMBERSHIP HAS BEEN ASSIGNE
      D, IT IS USEFUL TO EXCLUDE
 120  * ELEMENTS FROM CERTAIN SETS IN ORDER TO MANAGE MODEL SIZE.  FOR EXAMPLE, 
      ALL REGIONAL INPUTS ARE
 121  * ASSIGNED TO ALL REGIONS.  HOWEVER, IF SOME INPUTS ARE NOT USED IN SOME R
      EGIONS, THE NUMBER OF
 122  * CONSTRAINTS MAY BE REDUCED BY EXCLUDING THE INPUTS FROM THOSE REGIONS.
 123   
