1025  * REGIONAL AND NONREGIONAL PRODUCTS HAVE DEMAND ACTIVITIES.  SINCE THE OBJ
      ECTIVE FUNCTION OF THE MODEL
1026  * IS CONSUMER PLUS PRODUCER SURPLUS, THE OBJECTIVE FUNCTION ENTRY FOR A PR
      ODUCT DEMAND ACTIVITY IS THE
1027  * DEMAND FUNCTION INTEGRAL.  DEMAND FUNCTIONS ARE ASSUMED TO BE LINEAR, HO
      WEVER RELAXATION OF THAT
1028  * ASSUMPTION IS STRAIGHT FORWARD AND CAN BE ACCOMODATED WITH GAMS.  PARAME
      TERS ARE ASSIGNED OR COMPUTED
1029  * IN PRICE DEPENDENT FORM.  AN INFINITELY ELASTIC DEMAND IS INDICATED BY A
       ZERO SLOPE WITH THE INTERCEPT
1030  * THEN BECOMING THE CONSTANT MARKET PRICE.  IF IN THE FOLLOWING TABLES BOT
      H THE INTERCEPT AND SLOPE ARE
1031  * ZERO, OR EQUIVALENTLY BLANK, THE SLOPE AND INTERCEPT WILL BE COMPUTED WI
      TH THE USER ASSIGNED PRICE,
1032  * QUANTITY AND ELASTICITY (PBAR, QBAR AND ELAST, RESPECTIVELY) IF THE PBAR
       AND QBAR PARAMETERS ARE
1033  * POSITIVE AND THE ELAST PARAMETER IS NEGATIVE.
1034  *
1035  * FIXED DEMANDS CAN BE MODELED BY SETTING APPROPRIATE VALUES FOR QMIN AND 
      QMAX WHICH ARE USED AS LOWER
1036  * AND UPPER LIMITS, RESPECTIVELY, ON THE DEMAND ACTIVITIES.  IF EXOGENOUS 
      DEMAND FUNCTIONS ARE TO BE
1037  * USED WITHOUT OTHER LIMITS TO DEMAND, QMIN SHOULD BE SET TO ZERO AND QMAX
       SHOULD BE SET TO INFINITY
1038  * (INF).  A POSITIVE QMIN AND/OR A FINITE QMAX MAY BE SET, IF DESIRED, WIT
      H AN EXOGENOUS DEMAND FUNCTION
1039  * THAT IS PRICE RESPONSIVE OR INFINITELY ELASTIC FROM QMIN TO QMAX.
1040  *
1041  * PRICES ARE IN DOLLARS OR OTHER BASE CURRENCY USED IN THE MODEL.  QUANTIT
      IES ARE IN THE UNITS DEFINED
1042  * BY THE USER FOR THE PRODUCT'S DEMAND ACTIVITY AND CONSTRAINT.
