1352  * INPUT/OUTPUT COEFFICIENTS AND OTHER CONSTRAINT COEFFICIENTS FOR PRODUCTI
      ON ACTIVITIES MAY BE ENTERED
1353  * DIRECTLY, OR THEY MAY BE COMPUTED USING COEFFICIENTS FROM UNIT BUDGETS. 
       FOR CROP AND LIVESTOCK
1354  * PRODUCTION ACTIVITIES, THE CONSTRAINT COEFFICIENTS MAY BE COMPUTED WITH 
      COEFFICIENTS AND MULTIPLIERS
1355  * FOR RELATED CROP AND LIVESTOCK BUDGETS.
1356  *
1357  * THE INPUT/OUTPUT COEFFICIENTS SHOULD BE INTERPRETED AS THE NET USE OF TH
      E ITEM PER UNIT OF THE
1358  * ACTIVITY.  THUS AN INPUT REQUIREMENT WOULD BE INDICATED BY A POSITIVE CO
      EFFICIENT.  A NEGATIVE INPUT
1359  * COEFFICIENT IMPLIES THAT THE ACTIVITY IS A NET SUPPLIER OF THE INPUT.  A
       PRODUCT WOULD TYPICALLY HAVE
1360  * A NEGATIVE COEFFICIENT INDICATING NET SUPPLY.  ENDOGENOUS DEMAND FOR A P
      RODUCT WOULD BE IMPLIED BY A
1361  * PRODUCTION ACTIVITY WITH A POSITIVE INPUT COEFFICIENT.
